The governments of Nordinsel and Südinsel accuse one another of breaking promises in speeches – but their ambassadors continue negotiating. {{1}}
Nordinsel gathers troops at the border and openly threatens an invasion; talks have broken down. {{2}}
For months, there have been repeated exchanges of gunfire over a mountain pass on the border between Ostberg and Westberg. {{3}}
The armies of Rotland and Blauland have been fighting with tanks and aircraft over several regions for weeks. {{4}}
Two states argue bitterly in newspaper interviews over water rights on a border river – a mediator invites both to talks. {{5}}
After an incident at sea, Gelbland recalls its ambassador and puts its fleet on alert. {{6}}
In a border region, militias and government troops repeatedly clash – in the rest of the country, everyday life continues. {{7}}
Widespread air strikes hit targets across the country; both armies have been fighting continuously for months. {{8}}
A state bans entry to diplomats from its neighbouring country and issues a ‘final warning’. {{9}}
Two countries claim the same uninhabited group of islands and take the dispute to an international court. {{10}}
